[-46.076,-23.037],[-46.091,-23.066],[-46.09,-23.078],[-46.094,-23.084],[-46.105,-23.084],[-46.107,-23.096]]]},"wikidata":"Q191642","facts":{"population":{"value":727078,"year":2025},"founded":{"year":1767,"label":"1767"},"elevation":660,"officialArea":1099.77,"website":"http://www.sjc.sp.gov.br/"},"summary":{"extract":"São José dos Campos is a major city and the seat of the municipality of the same name in the state of São Paulo, Brazil. One of the leading industrial and research centers with emphasis in aerospace sciences in Latin America, the city is located in the Paraíba Valley, between the two most active production and consumption regions in the country; São Paulo and Rio de Janeiro. It is the main city of the Metropolitan Region of Vale do Paraíba e Litoral Norte. A native of São José dos Campos is called a joseense. Being the second most populous non-capital city in Brazil – behind Campinas – São José dos Campos lies in the middle of the Expanded Metropolitan Complex, the first megalopolis in the Southern Hemisphere, with over thirty million inhabitants. The city's metro area also includes Greater São Paulo, Campinas, Santos and Sorocaba.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/SJos%C3%A9Campos.jpg/330px-SJos%C3%A9Campos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Jos%C3%A9_dos_Campos"},"twins":["Q496080","Q199440"],"climate":{"temp":[23.6,23.6,22.9,21.3,18.4,17.7,17.4,18.9,21.1,22.6,22.5,23.4],"rain":[239,178,149,80,64,45,49,33,61,109,162,197],"cloud":[76,67,66,61,62,54,50,50,63,72,77,78]}}